<h2>NBA Standing Reach — The Number That Matters More Than Vertical</h2>
<p>Standing reach — how high a player can touch flat-footed with one arm extended — is arguably more important than vertical jump for basketball, yet it's discussed far less. It determines how high a player can reach <em>before</em> jumping at all, which affects rebounding, shot-blocking, and finishing.</p>
