<p>The average NBA standing reach is approximately <strong>8 feet 6 inches</strong>. Since the rim sits at 10 feet, the average NBA player needs only about an 18-inch vertical to touch the rim, and roughly a 24-inch vertical to dunk comfortably. This is why standing reach matters so much: a player with a 9-foot standing reach and a modest vertical can dunk more easily than a player with an 8-foot reach and an explosive vertical. LeBron James's 8'10.5" standing reach is a major reason he finishes so effectively at the rim even as his vertical has declined with age.</p>
